    {
      "text": "There's a moment at the end of a meal where the bill arrives, and everyone at the table does the same quiet calculation. Who earns what? Who can afford what? Who ordered the steak and who ordered the soup? Nobody says any of it out loud, but everybody is doing the maths. Now imagine that calculation is unnecessary, because the moment you sat down, above your head, in numbers everyone can read, was the exact amount of money in your bank account. For about a day, people treated it like a novelty. By Thursday, nobody in the country was lying about money anymore. Not because they'd become honest, because they couldn't. This is what actually happens when the last private number in your life becomes public.",
      "start_time": 0.16,
      "end_time": 44.38,
      "speaker": {
        "id": "speaker_0",
        "name": "Speaker 0"
      },
